A||||3||FieroLisa||Great car show this weekend!||||1||
Z||000000||FieroLisa||05-06-2001||11:32 AM||||I went to a car show this weekend in Indianapolis at Tom Wood Pontiac...the show was excellent! It was all Pontiacs, and had 4 classes- GTO, Firebird/TA, Classics and FIERO! 7 Fieros showed up, all in great shape. They handed out 3 trophies in each class. For the Fieros, 3rd place went a white coupe in excellent shape, I got 2nd (my cars first trophy!!) and Chris got first with his convertible N*. He also got best engineered car out of the entire show. <BR>So some people do have respect for Fieros as show cars!<P>The trophies were great too...I didn't see what 3rd place got, but 2nd got 2 etched glasses that said the name of the show, Second Place, and Fiero Class. First place trophies were amazing...It was a little stand with the top surface mirrored with a hole in it...another piece of crystal with the show info and placing lay over that space and under it there was a revolving, different colored light. I can't even explain it, but it was sweet!<P>So anyway, I strongly recommend anyone making the drive to the show next year, nice people, nice fieros, nice tropies! <BR>And it only cost a $10 entry fee which I believe went to a charity anyway. Much better than the show I went to last weekend in Cinci where I paid $20 and didn't even get judged (I'm still hostile over that)<P><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT- 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air,<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||05-06-2001||06:02 PM||||good going lisa !!!!! what time did you get back? I went to a show in Mt Vernon and ran into Tweety and her hubby. Noticed you put on some temp seat covers, looks pretty nice.||||reg||1
Z||000002||JJ-85-2M6||05-06-2001||06:58 PM|||| I thought that might be the show you were going to in Indy.  It must have really grown.  I went there (no car)in 1999 and there was only 1 Fiero. Sounds like it was fun!  Tom Wood was my dealership when I lived in Indy and I bought my original Fiero there in 1985! Don Sisk Pontiac (West side of Indy) has a similar show June 2(?).  They had 7 or so Fieros there in 2000.   ||||reg||14
Z||000003||FieroLisa||05-06-2001||08:29 PM||||roger: got back around 4. nice that you leave your hose on 24/7 cause I had to get rid of all the indiana bugs off my front end!  yah I was trying to put some nice GT seats in my car for the show but found out that apparently my car got into a bad enough accident once upon a time to bend the frame and therefoer a seat from another fiero won't fit right. grrrr. So i got those seat covers until I order my leather ones.||||reg||1
